Executive Order 1019.wikitext:
{{TextQuality|75%}}{{Potus-eo
 | eo       = 1019
 | section  = Establishing Hawaiian Islands Reservation as Preserve and Breeding Ground for Native Birds
 | year     = 1909
 | month    = 2
 | day      = 3
 | notes    = Renamed by [[Proclamation 2416]], July 25, 1940.
}}

It is hereby ordered that the following islets and reefs, namely: [[w:Kure Atoll|Cure Island]], [[w:Pearl and Hermes Atoll|Pearl and Hermes Reef]], [[w:Lisianski Island|Lysianski]] or Pell Island, [[w:Laysan|Laysan]] Island, [[w:Maro Reef|Mary Reef]], Dowsetts Reef, [[w:Gardner Pinnacles|Gardiner Island]], Two Brothers Reef, [[w:French Frigate Shoals|French Frigate Shoal]], [[w:Necker Island (Northwestern Hawaiian Islands)|Necker Island]], Frost Shoal and [[w:Nihoa|Bird Island]], situated in the Pacific Ocean at and near the extreme western extension of the Hawaiian Archipelago between latitudes 23° and 29° north, and longitudes 160° and 180° west from Greenwich, and located within the area segregated by the broken lines shown upon the diagram hereto [[#Annex|attached]] and made a part of this order, are hereby reserved and set apart, subject to valid existing rights, for the use of the Department of Agriculture as a preserve and breeding ground for native birds. It is unlawful for any person to hunt, trap, capture, wilfully disturb, or kill any bird of any kind whatever, or take the eggs of such birds within the limits of this reservation except under such rules and regulations as may be prescribed from time to time by the Secretary of Agriculture. Warning is expressly given to all persons not to commit any of the acts herein enumerated and which are prohibited by law.


This reservation to be known as the [[w:Hawaiian Islands National Wildlife Refuge|Hawaiian Islands Reservation]].

<div style="text-align:right">[[File:Theodore Roosevelt Signature.svg|Signature of Theodore Roosevelt|170px]]<br/>
{{sc|Theodore Roosevelt}}.</div>
{{sc|The White House}}
::''February 3, 1909.''


